# Stakeholder-Anchored Development — Archangel methodology rule (pack `sad@0.1.0`)

> Synthesised by Archangel. To remove cleanly:
> `archangel methodology unsync-host --pack sad --host cursor`
> Hand edits to this file are clobbered on next sync — clone the file under a different name to fork.

## Lifecycle phases

- [ ] **brainstorm** (1) — Brainstorm
- [ ] **specify** (2) — Specify
- [ ] **clarify** (3) — Clarify
- [ ] **impact-forecast** (4) — Impact Forecast
- [ ] **plan** (5) — Plan
- [ ] **walkthrough** (6) — Walkthrough (tier-routed approval)
- [ ] **analyze** (7) — Analyze
- [ ] **tasks** (8) — Tasks
- [ ] **implement** (9) — Implement
- [ ] **review** (10) — Review
- [ ] **reconcile** (11) — Reconcile
- [ ] **compound** (12) — Compound (lessons)

## Working under this methodology

1. The active workspace is matched against `specs/*/**` (see manifest).
2. Each spec dir contains its own `tasks.md` (or pack-declared lifecycle file).
3. Out-of-scope edits surface as drift events in Archangel.
4. When proposing changes, name the active spec and lifecycle phase.
